\par }{\b\insrsid6832331 Overview}{\b\insrsid6832331\charrsid6832331 
\par }{\insrsid6832331 
\par }{\insrsid14755328 To assist research focusing on interstate dyads, we have converted the alliance data set into two auxiliary (dyadic-annual) files.  These files contain information \endash  on an annual basis \endash 
 as to the alliance relationship between any two states.  All dyad-years where some alliance tie is present are contained in these files \endash  if a dyad-year is not listed, then there is no formal alliance between the two states in that year.}{
\insrsid1912714   When alliance membership changed during the year (e.g. if a country left an alliance on some date while the alliance itself continued, or }{\insrsid3960424 it }{\insrsid1912714 joined after the initial date of alliance creation)}{
\insrsid13769774 , a check was performed to ensure that the }{\insrsid3960424 dyad members}{\insrsid13769774  were members of the alliance for at least one common day.  If they were, then a record }{\insrsid3960424 showing an alliance status }{
\insrsid13769774 for the year was created.}{\insrsid14755328 
\par 
\par The dyadic alliance data are presented in two formats, one with one record per dyad-year (listing the }{\insrsid3960424 greatest}{\insrsid14755328  level }{\insrsid3960424 of }{\insrsid14755328 
alliance commitment between the states in that year), and one with multiple records per dyad year (each record listing one alliance between the states in that year).  
\par }{\insrsid993893 
\par }{\insrsid6832331 
\par }{\b\insrsid993893\charrsid993893 Current Version and Updates:
\par }{\insrsid993893 
\par The current version for the multiple-observation-per-year data set is v3.0}{\insrsid7869188 3}{\insrsid993893 .  This data set }{\insrsid7869188 was created after the main alliance data set was updated to v3.03.  }{\insrsid14755328 
\par }{\insrsid993893 
\par }{\insrsid7869188 The current version for the single-observation-per-year data set is v3.03.  This data set was created after the main alliance data set was updated to v3.03.  
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid993893 {\i\insrsid7869188\charrsid7869188 Previous update}{\insrsid7869188 :  Previously, }{\insrsid993893 v3.02}{\insrsid7869188  of the dyadic 
single-observation-per-year was created to replace the v3.01 version }{\insrsid993893 to correct an error in the creation of the one-observation-per-year data.  In v3.0 and 3.01, a handful of d
yad year observations (approximately 40 out of 68,000 dyad-years) were mistakenly dropped because of a programming error.  The cases dropped were essentially random (technically, they were dropped because of a sorting error; cases dropped were cases where
 an alliance in one dyad started in the same year that the alliance in the previous dyad ended).  v3.01 contained 88371 ob}{\insrsid7869188 s}{\insrsid993893 ervations; v3.02 contain}{\insrsid7869188 ed}{\insrsid993893  }{\insrsid7436077 88412}{
\insrsid993893  observations.  The new data set contains all dyad-year observations, without this drop error.
\par 
\par }{\insrsid6832331 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx1083\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6832331 {\b\insrsid6832331\charrsid2693417 Note on file formats and reading data into software:}{\b\insrsid6832331 
\par }{\b\insrsid6832331\charrsid2693417 
\par }{\insrsid6832331 These data sets are both in comma-delimited ascii format;  that is, values are separated by commas.  By default in Microsoft Windows, files with a .csv extension will be opened in Microsoft Excel.  However, Ex
cel only allows spreadsheets with up to 65535 rows of data.  Both of these files contain more records than this.  To access these datasets, you should use a statistics program such as SPSS or Stata (for instance, using Stata\rquote s \'93insheet\'94 
command) to correctly access the full data. }{\insrsid6832331\charrsid14755328 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid993893 {\insrsid6832331 
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\insrsid13769774 Data set 1:  }{\b\insrsid14755328\charrsid14755328 Multiple }{\b\insrsid13769774 r}{\b\insrsid14755328\charrsid14755328 ecords per dyad year (alliance_v3}
{\b\insrsid7815766 .}{\b\insrsid14755328\charrsid14755328 0}{\b\insrsid7869188 3}{\b\insrsid14755328\charrsid14755328 _annual_dyadic_multiple.csv)  
\par }{\insrsid14755328 
\par Contains multiple records per dyad year.  In this file, }{\insrsid1912714 the unit of observation is the nondirected-dyad-alliance-year}{\insrsid16059345 , but with both directions of the dyad listed}{\insrsid1912714 .  }{\insrsid16059345 In this file, }{
\ul\insrsid14755328\charrsid3960424 each}{\insrsid14755328  }{\ul\insrsid14755328\charrsid3960424 alliance }{\insrsid14755328 between the members of a dyad that is active in a given year has }{\insrsid16059345 a separate }{\insrsid14755328 
record.  So, if ccode 300 is a member of alliance #5 (which also contains ccode 255) in 1840, and ccode 300 is also a member of alliance #7 (which also contains ccode 255) in 1840, then two output records will be created for }{\insrsid16059345 
dyad 300 255 in }{\insrsid14755328 1840, one listing alliance 5, the second listing alliance 7.}{\insrsid16059345   
\par 
\par Note that while the data is at root nondirected \endash  meaning that an alliance between ccode 300 and 255 in a given year is the same as the listed alliance between 255 and 300 \endash 
 both directions of each dyad are reported.  That is, there is a record for 255 300 1840 (e.g.), and for 300 255 1840, in the data set.  If you wish to have a completely nondirected dyad data set, with only one direction of each dyad in each year}{
\insrsid11757081  in the typical format where ccode1 should always be less than ccode2}{\insrsid16059345 , simply use a command to drop one of the directions, such as (in Stata) \'93drop if ccode1 > ccode2.\'94  }{\insrsid14755328 
\par 
\par }{\i\insrsid14755328\charrsid14755328 Variables}{\i\insrsid14755328  and Format
